    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The railroad arrived in Phillipsport in 1899, signaling the end of the Delaware and Hudson Canal’s era in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mamakating%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Phillipsport is listed in both the FIPS‑55 and GNIS databases, confirming its official status as a recognized place.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://roadsidethoughts.com/ny/phillipsport-xx-sullivan-profile.htm"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Phillipsport lies in southeastern Sullivan County, New York, near the historic Old Mine Road that once linked Kingston to the Hudson Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mamakating%2C_New_York"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town of Mamakating, which contains Phillipsport, was organized in 1743 as part of Ulster County before becoming the first town in Sullivan County.",
